    {
      "phase": "phase_4_sentiment_rebuild",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-11T13:40:58.522402+00:00",
      "note": "Rebuilt Sentiment Analyst on a single combined social score merging Twitter/X cashtag search + Reddit (WSB/stocks/investing) + StockTwits stream, deliberately NOT split into 3 separate averaged agents. Simulated random sentiment/volume/trend generation removed entirely. Verified the StockTwits path (keyless) actually attempts a real network call and correctly degrades on the same 403 policy denial seen from every other financial host in this session, rather than short-circuiting on a missing-key check alone. Also fixed a real perf bug found while running this: base_client.py previously had no negative cache, so every degraded call retried full exponential backoff -- harmless for a single call, but would have made both this diagnostic (thousands of trials) and a real backtest (one evaluation per symbol-day) unusably slow against a persistently-down feed. Added a short-TTL negative cache (60s) so a dead feed's retry cost is paid once, not every call.",
